# Per-sleeve kill-switch — the SINGLE source of truth for which strategy sleeves run.
#
# Flip a sleeve to "off" and redeploy to retire it. Unlike `systemctl disable` by hand
# (which the next deploy silently re-enables), this SURVIVES deploys: the deploy enables
# only the "on" sleeves and `disable --now`s the "off" ones, and the verify + the liveness
# watchdog stop expecting them.
#
# SAFETY — what "off" does and does NOT do:
#   * "off" stops the sleeve's daemon -> NO NEW entries.
#   * It does NOT flatten open positions. Protection depends on the active profile:
#     LONG uses venue-managed exits, while the current continuous profile is deliberately
#     stopless and relies on TP/max-hold plus ws_risk lifecycle monitoring. Treat any open
#     position as remaining risk; verify its actual venue protection and wind the sleeve
#     flat BEFORE considering it retired.
#   * EXCEPTION — the continuous HEDGE leg. The 2f BTC/ETH hedge long is booked STOPLESS
#     (stop_price=0) on purpose: the risk service tracks but never force-exits it, and its
#     ONLY manager is the periodic hedge timer, which rides CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE. Flipping
#     CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=off with an open hedge leg leaves a permanently-open, unmanaged
#     position. FLATTEN the hedge (or keep CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE on until the hedge ledger is
#     flat) before retiring continuous. The liveness watchdog now pages CRITICAL
#     ("ORPHANED HEDGE") if it sees an open hedge leg while the hedge timer is disabled.
#   * The risk service itself has no toggle: it always runs and keeps reading every
#     configured ledger root.
#
# Accepted values: on | off  (also 1/true/yes == on). Per-host overrides live in
# /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.env, but they can only NARROW a repo-on sleeve
# to off. A repo-side off is a hard ceiling and a stale host "on" cannot resurrect it.
# Deploy writes the final resolved values to /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.resolved.env
# for systemd units to consume.
#
# Plain KEY=value (no shell ${:-} expansion) so this file is valid as BOTH a bash `source`
# (deploy/verify) AND a systemd EnvironmentFile (the liveness watchdog reads the toggles to
# skip an intentionally-off sleeve). Keep it that way.

# LONG   = long-native v11a: demo + paper services (a diversifier overlay). FORWARD-DEMO STARTED
# 2026-06-04 on this box (first time). "on" shares the one netted demo
# account's margin with the continuous sleeve (no budget throttle). Flip to off to retire it; open demo
# positions then ride to natural exit under the always-on risk service (no flatten).
# RE-ENABLED 2026-06-16 by operator. Runs the v11a demo unit: SUBMIT_ORDERS=1,
# ENTRY_LEVERAGE=10, capped at MAX_PROJECTED_INITIAL_MARGIN_PCT_EQUITY=0.5, on the SAME
# netted demo account as the (now actively-trading) continuous sleeve. Demo only,
# REAL_MONEY=false. The STATE.md "LONG leverage/capital" decision = this current sizing.
LONG_SLEEVE=on
# CONTINUOUS = continuous-fade DEMO order-submitting sleeve.
# ON 2026-06-09 by EXPLICIT operator instruction; LONG was re-enabled 2026-06-16.
# This sleeve runs continuous demo orders + paper shadow to accumulate forward
# evidence and observed-fill cost calibration. Demo account only (REAL_MONEY=false);
# demo fills are execution evidence, not alpha proof. The current
# continuous_ensemble_v2 profile includes the 2026-06-25
# CTRL_BTC_RISK_70_90_35 BTC-risk sizing override. The rmom panel is the
# post-look-ahead-fix shift3 causal build.
CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=on
# CONTINUOUS_PAPER = no-order paper shadow of the demo book (the unit pins
# STRATEGY_PROFILE=continuous_ensemble_v2, mirroring demo). This can run while
# CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE stays off: SUBMIT_ORDERS=0, RECORD_DRY_RUN=1, PAPER_MODE=1.
# It feeds paper/demo reconciliation and execution-drift evidence without touching the demo account.
CONTINUOUS_PAPER_SLEEVE=on
